  "id": "ghsl",
  "title": "GHSL Population Grids (GHS-POP R2023A)",
  "description": "A cloud-native mirror of the European Commission Joint Research Centre's GHS-POP R2023A population grids: twelve five-yearly epochs from 1975 to 2030 at 100 m in World Mollweide (ESRI:54009). The upstream rasters are stored in Deflated ZIP members without internal overviews, preventing partial reads over HTTP. This mirror converts them to Cloud Optimized GeoTIFFs with overviews and embedded statistics. It is a derived, lossy product: pixel values are quantized to 0.01 persons per cell and are not bit-identical to JRC's distribution. The grid, model, inputs, authors, and licence are unchanged. See the [catalog agent guide](AGENTS.md) for query recipes and [why this mirror exists](https://github.com/nlebovits/ghsl/blob/main/docs/upstream-gaps.md) for measurements.",
